                     <value>*</value>
                  </upperValue>
                  <name>publishingPrinciples</name>
                  <type xmi:idref="DiscoveryDataDescriptionStructure.Reference"/>
               </ownedAttribute>
               <ownedAttribute xmi:id="DiscoveryDataDescriptionStructure.Dataset-keywords" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/data_structure/1.1/composite/xmi/#Dataset-keywords" xmi:type="uml:Property">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="DiscoveryDataDescriptionStructure.Dataset-keywords-ownedComment" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/data_structure/1.1/composite/xmi/#Dataset-keywords-ownedComment" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="DiscoveryDataDescriptionStructure.Dataset-keywords"/>
                     <body>Documentation
=============

Original
--------

Reference
.........
schema:keywords

Definition
..........
Keywords or tags used to describe some item. Multiple textual entries in a keywords list are typically delimited by commas, or by repeating the property.

Scope
.....
Domain: CreativeWork (https://schema.org/CreativeWork), Event (https://schema.org/Event), Organization (https://schema.org/Organization), Place (https://schema.org/Place), Product (https://schema.org/Product).
Range: DefinedTerm (https://schema.org/DefinedTerm), Text (https://schema.org/Text), URL (https://schema.org/URL).


CDIF
----

Definition
..........
Keywords are an array of strings, an array of schema:DefinedTerms, or some combination of these. If you have information about a controlled vocabulary from which keywords come from, use schema:DefinedTerm to descibe that keyword. This allowed variability makes parsing metadata hard; recommend using DefinedTerm for all keywords if any of them are from a known vocabulary, otherwise an array of strings.

Scope
.....
schema:keywords - keywords as strings or DefinedTerms.
</body>
                  </ownedComment>
