schema:provider

Definition
..........
The service provider, service operator, or service performer; the goods producer. Another party (a seller) may offer those services or goods on behalf of the provider. A provider may also serve as the seller.

Scope
.....
Domain: Action (https://schema.org/Action), CreativeWork (https://schema.org/CreativeWork), EducationalOccupationalProgram (https://schema.org/EducationalOccupationalProgram), FinancialIncentive (https://schema.org/FinancialIncentive), Invoice (https://schema.org/Invoice), ParcelDelivery (https://schema.org/ParcelDelivery), Reservation (https://schema.org/Reservation), Service (https://schema.org/Service), Trip (https://schema.org/Trip).
Range: Organization (https://schema.org/Organization), Person (https://schema.org/Person).


CDIF
----

Definition
..........
Party who maintains the distribution options for the dataset. If there are multiple distributions from different providers, use the provider property on distribution/DataDownload

Scope
.....
schema:provider - the agent providing access to the dataset. The Agent supertype admits Person or Organization.
</body>
